{
  "id": "PSI-23",
  "summary_plain": "This investigation burns gaseous fuel and diluent mixtures through a spherical porous burner inside the International Space Station's Combustion Integrated Rack to create spherical diffusion flames. By studying these flames in microgravity without buoyancy, researchers can rigorously test detailed numerical models of chemical kinetics and radiation. This work helps improve combustion efficiency and safety for both Earth systems and spacecraft.",
  "summary_expert": "The ACME s-Flame investigation utilizes the Combustion Integrated Rack (CIR) on the International Space Station to study the structure and response of spherical diffusion flames. Gaseous fuels including hydrogen, methane, and ethylene are mixed with diluents such as nitrogen, helium, and carbon dioxide, and issued through a spherical porous burner into an oxidizing environment. Variables examined include fuel-to-diluent ratios, flow rates, and reactant compositions for both soot-free and sooty flames to determine transient flame structures, convective/chemical-kinetic and radiative/chemical-kinetic extinction limits, and pulsating instabilities. The resulting data provide a rigorous test of comprehensive numerical simulations incorporating detailed chemistry and transport models.",
  "key_findings": [
    {
      "text": "On GMT 136, 11 flames were successfully ignited for ACME s-Flame burning a hydrogen/methane fuel mixture diluted with helium at a specific flammable gas ratio.",
      "source": {
        "psi_id": "PSI-23",
        "doi": "10.60555/k57n-p030",
        "file": "documents/PSI-23/PSI-23_Reports_s_Flame_final_report_20210729.pdf",
        "page": 81
      },
      "provenance": "Google Gemini (free tier)"
    },
    {
      "text": "The flames all radiatively extinguished, but no sooting was observed.",
      "source": {
        "psi_id": "PSI-23",
        "doi": "10.60555/k57n-p030",
        "file": "documents/PSI-23/PSI-23_Reports_s_Flame_final_report_20210729.pdf",
        "page": 43
      },
      "provenance": "quoted from PSI document (rules, no LLM)"
    },
    {
      "text": "As for cases where the flow rates were ramped down, extinction detection was observed for both oxygen concentration environments.",
